/-!
# Homotopies of morphisms of simplicial objects

Homotopies between morphisms of simplicial objects, the relations satisfied by their components,
their preservation by functors, homotopy equivalences, and the category of homotopy classes of
morphisms.
-/

/-!
## Homotopies of simplicial objects

Let `C` be a category and let `U`, `V` be simplicial objects of `C`. Write `U × Δ[1]` for the
product of `U` with the standard `1`-simplex, the simplicial object `m ↦ ∐_{α ∈ Δ[1]_m} U_m`
of [Stacks, Tag 017C] (`CategoryTheory.Functor.copower`); it exists as soon as those
coproducts do, in particular whenever `C` has finite coproducts, each set `Δ[1]_m` being
finite and nonempty. The two vertices `e₀, e₁ : Δ[0] ⟶ Δ[1]` together with the identification
`U × Δ[0] = U` produce two morphisms `e₀, e₁ : U ⟶ U × Δ[1]`, and a morphism
`h : U × Δ[1] ⟶ V` is a *homotopy from `a` to `b`*, for `a, b : U ⟶ V`, when `a = e₀ ≫ h` and
`b = e₁ ≫ h`. Two morphisms `a`, `b` are *homotopic*, or *in the same homotopy class*, when
they are related by the equivalence relation generated by "there is a homotopy from `a` to
`b`"; the generating relation is in general neither symmetric nor transitive, though it is
reflexive ([Stacks, Tag 07KA]).

### Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.IsHomotopy`: `IsHomotopy h a b` says that the morphism
  `h : U × Δ[1] ⟶ V` is a homotopy from `a` to `b`, that is, `a = e₀ ≫ h` and `b = e₁ ≫ h`.

### Implementation notes

Being homotopic, part (2) of the source's definition, is the equivalence relation generated by
part (1), as the source itself observes: for `a b : U ⟶ V` it is
`Relation.EqvGen (fun a b ↦ ∃ h, IsHomotopy h a b) a b`, the chains `a = a₀, a₁, …, a_n = b` of the
source being the constructors `Relation.EqvGen.symm` and `Relation.EqvGen.trans` applied to
`Relation.EqvGen.rel`.

### References

* [Stacks, Tag 019K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/019K)
-/

section

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Simplicial SSet

universe w v u

namespace CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {U V : SimplicialObject C}
  [∀ m, HasCoproduct fun _ : (Δ[1] : SSet.{w}).obj m => U.obj m]

/-- **Stacks 019K** (part 1).
Given simplicial objects `U`, `V` of a category `C` for which the product
`U × Δ[1] = U.copower Δ[1]` of [Stacks, Tag 017C] exists, a morphism `h : U × Δ[1] ⟶ V` is a
*homotopy from `a` to `b`* for `a, b : U ⟶ V` when `a = e₀ ≫ h` and `b = e₁ ≫ h`, where
`e₀, e₁ : U ⟶ U × Δ[1]` come from the two vertices `Δ[0] ⟶ Δ[1]` and the identification
`U × Δ[0] = U`. In degree `m` these two vertex inclusions are the inclusions of the summands of
`∐_{α ∈ Δ[1]_m} U_m` indexed by the constant `m`-simplices `SSet.stdSimplex.const 1 0 m` and
`SSet.stdSimplex.const 1 1 m` of `Δ[1]`, which is how the two conditions are spelled here;
equivalently, `h_{m, m + 1} = a_m` and `h_{m, 0} = b_m` in the notation of [Stacks, Tag 019L]. -/
@[stacks 019K "part (1); part (2), being homotopic, is the equivalence relation \
  `Relation.EqvGen (fun a b ↦ ∃ h, IsHomotopy h a b)` generated by it, see the module docstring",
  sga "4 Vbis 3.0.2"]
public def IsHomotopy (h : U.copower Δ[1] ⟶ V) (a b : U ⟶ V) : Prop :=
  (∀ m, Sigma.ι (fun _ : (Δ[1] : SSet.{w}).obj m => U.obj m) (stdSimplex.const 1 0 m) ≫
      h.app m = a.app m) ∧
  (∀ m, Sigma.ι (fun _ : (Δ[1] : SSet.{w}).obj m => U.obj m) (stdSimplex.const 1 1 m) ≫
      h.app m = b.app m)

end CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject

end

end

/-!
## The relations satisfied by the components of a homotopy

Let `C` be a category and let `U`, `V` be simplicial objects of `C` for which the product
`U × Δ[1] = U.copower Δ[1]` of [Stacks, Tag 017C] exists. Its `n`-th term is the coproduct of
copies of `U_n` indexed by the `n`-simplices of `Δ[1]`, that is by `Hom_Δ(⦋n⦌, ⦋1⦌)`, and a
homotopy from `a : U ⟶ V` to `b : U ⟶ V` is a morphism `h : U × Δ[1] ⟶ V` with `e_0 ≫ h = a` and
`e_1 ≫ h = b` ([Stacks, Tag 019K], `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.IsHomotopy`), where `e_0`
and `e_1 : U ⟶ U × Δ[1]` are the inclusions of the summands indexed by the constant simplices of
value `0` and of value `1`. The `n`-simplices of `Δ[1]` are the `n + 2` simplices
`α^n_i = SSet.stdSimplex.objMk₁ i`, the monotone maps `⦋n⦌ ⟶ ⦋1⦌` taking the value `0` on
`{j | j < i}` and the value `1` on `{j | i ≤ j}`, so `h` is determined by its components
`h_{n, i} : U_n ⟶ V_n`, the restrictions of `h_n` to the summands. A family of morphisms
`h_{n, i}` is the family of components of a homotopy from `a` to `b` exactly when it satisfies
five relations against the face maps `d^n_j` and the degeneracy maps `s^n_j`, and then the
homotopy is unique.

### Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.homotopyComponent`: the component `h_{n, i} : U_n ⟶ V_n` of
  `h : U × Δ[1] ⟶ V`, the restriction of `h_n` to the summand indexed by `α^n_i`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.HtpyRel`: the five relations tying a family of morphisms
  `h_{n, i} : U_n ⟶ V_n` to `a`, `b` and the face and degeneracy maps of `U` and `V`.

### Main results

* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.htpy_forward`: the components of a homotopy from `a` to `b`
  satisfy `HtpyRel a b`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.htpy_converse`: a family satisfying `HtpyRel a b` is the
  family of components of a unique morphism `U × Δ[1] ⟶ V`, and that morphism is a homotopy
  from `a` to `b`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.htpy_converse_exists`: a family satisfying `HtpyRel a b` is
  the family of components of some homotopy from `a` to `b`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.htpy_converse_unique`: two morphisms `U × Δ[1] ⟶ V` with the
  same components are equal.

### References

* [Stacks, Tag 019L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/019L)
-/

